<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (Twenty years of foils, in one system)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (Manta Foils has been designing foils since before most riders had heard of them. Our founder Renaud Barbier built his first kitefoil prototype in 2002, produced some of the first commercial kitefoils in 2011, then launched one of the first aluminium foils, the first inflatable foil board, early wings and early eFoils. Foil, board, motor, battery, electronics, software: for more than 20 years almost every part has been designed in-house. The TakeOff Evo is where all of that comes together.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
124 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (It is the lightest and most compact Foil Assist we have built, and one of the most powerful on the market. Its fully enclosed motor delivers 3,500 W and needs almost no care: rinse it for a few seconds and ride again. No spray, no rusting parts, no bearings to replace. That power is what lets you ride smaller wings and smaller boards, and gets heavier riders flying.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
125 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (The batteries decide how you ride. A light Air battery for effortless pumping and hard carving. Bigger Ultra & Endurance batteries for long sessions in the waves or in eFoil mode. Plug them together for up to 1200 Wh. And because each Air pack stays under 100 Wh, the Evo is still the only Foil Assist you can fly with carrying several batteries. Your holiday does not stop after one session.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
126 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (The remote has riding profiles and gears to make the first sessions easier and the later ones faster, with GPS tracking of every ride in the Manta app.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (Most of what is in the Evo came from riders telling us what they wanted. Keep telling us.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
